To create a web page that displays an image with a caption underneath it using HTML and CSS, you can follow these steps:

### HTML Code

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Image with Caption</title>
    <style>
        /* Style for the container holding the image */
        .container {
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            width: 100%;
            padding-top: 20px; /* Add some space above the image */
        }

        /* Styling for the image itself */
        .container img {
            max-width: 100%;
            height: auto;
        }

        /* Styling for the caption */
        .caption {
            color: white;
            background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7);
            border-radius: 5px;
            padding: 10px;
            margin-top: -20px; /* Adjust based on your layout requirements */
            position: relative;
            left: calc((100% - 300px) / 2); /* Center the caption horizontally */
        }

        /* Styling for the link (optional) */
        .link {
            text-decoration: none;
            color: inherit;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="container">
    <a href="http://www.example.com" class="link">Click Here To View Image</a>
    <img src="image.jpg" alt="Sample Image">
    <div class="caption">This is a sample caption.</div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation of CSS Styles:

1. **Container**: The `.container` uses Flexbox to center the image both vertically and horizontally within its parent element.
   ```css
   .container {
       display: flex;
       align-items: center;
       justify-content: center;
       width: 100%;
       padding-top: 20px; /* Optional spacing around the image */
   }
   ```

2. **Image**: Ensures the image scales correctly while maintaining its aspect ratio.
   ```css
   .container img {
       max-width: 100%;
       height: auto;
   }
   ```

3. **Caption**: A semi-transparent box positioned below the image. It includes a hover effect to reveal more details if needed.
   ```css
   .caption {
       color: white;
       background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7);
       border-radius: 5px;
       padding: 10px;
       margin-top: -20px; /* Adjust based on your layout requirements */
       position: relative;
       left: calc((100% - 300px) / 2); /* Center the caption horizontally */
   }
   ```

4. **Link**: Optionally styled as a link that users can click to view more information about the image.

### How to Use:
1. Replace `"image.jpg"` with the actual URL or path of your image file.
2. Customize the `alt` attribute of the `<img>` tag to describe what's inside the image.
3. Adjust the styling as necessary to fit into your website design.

This setup provides a clean, centered presentation of the image with a caption, making it easy for users to navigate between the image and additional information.

